; with matrix literals (matrix.kurt), an operator bound to `multiply` can't be `sym`: the factors
; would be sorted, and the true product `[[1, 2], [3, 4]] * [[0, 1], [1, 0]] = [[2, 1], [4, 3]]`
; rejected while the swapped one is accepted (2026-10-15, the theories' audit)
load matrix, logic
infix * 70 70
expect "EvalError" "commutative"
    sym *
    builtin * multiply
infix ** 70 70
builtin ** multiply
expect "EvalError" "commutative"
    sym **
